    {
      "sheet": "Front Door Woofer",
      "range": "A2:H6",
      "values": [
        [
          "The front door woofer in the B&O system is an 8 ohm 4\"x6\" rear firing woofer rated at 100W.  Actual amp output unknown.  The door woofer has a 8.5\" bolt circle, but an 8\" woofer will just barely not fit under the door shroud unless you grind a couple flats onto the top and bottom edges.",
          null,
          null,
          null,
          null,
          null,
          null,
          null
        ],
        [
          "The factory door woofer channel is driven to 44Hz. Replacement speaker should be able to play this low, and you may want to add an amp with a low pass filter to the subwoofer. The factory door grill substantially limits the door woofer.  I doubled the number of holes in mine which helped.",
          null,
          null,
          null,
          null,
          null,
          null,
          null
        ],
        [
          "Installing generous Dynamat under the rear seat will substantially improve the performance of the front door woofers, especially on the S models as road and exhaust noise in the midbass range gets into the car through the rear seat.",
          null,
          null,
